# CO-439 — defense in depth (NOT a security boundary).
#
# The real boundary is the serve allowlist (co-web/src/server/allowlist.rs):
# the surfaces server serves only indexed/published entries, never raw disk
# files. This denylist is a cheap, complementary second layer that keeps known
# draft/scratch categories out of the build context entirely. A denylist FAILS
# OPEN — anything it does not list still ships — so never rely on it alone.
#
# Patterns below match the draft categories that appeared in the 2026-06
# ArteLonga/yuri "thrive market.md" leak post-mortem.

# Build artifacts / deps
target/
**/target/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.git/

# Draft / scratch naming conventions (one line each)
WhatsApp*
_*
shot-*
*.mov
**/IMG_*

# Local env / editor noise
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
